Amy: Customer (acct: acme-42) reports SSE disconnect mid-stream when switching from WiFi -> cellular during a long generation. They see socket close + client error: "EOF" and server logs show a 401 for the final resume chunk.

Jordan: Can you paste the minimal logs? want request ids.

Amy: paste: "req=R-7f9c auth=eyJ... refresh=ok event=stream_chunk id=chunk_24 -> client_closed: ECONNRESET" then 1s later "req=R-7f9c auth=eyJ... new_token refresh start" and server emits "401 session mismatch". Customer says it happens only on mobile handoffs.

Tom: Mobile note: iOS/WebKit aggressively retires sockets on network handover. If token refresh spawns a new connection and we cancel the old, the in-flight stream can be interrupted. Often the app restarts SSE with a new Authorization header which may trigger server-side session verification rejecting leftover state.

Rene: Hypothesis: token refresh race + server conservative session bound -> when new token is issued we mark old authorization invalid causing in-flight SSE to be rejected on the broker side. Need trace of auth ids and token jti.

Amy: Repro steps I gave customer:
1) Start SSE generation (long response > 30s)
2) Force network switch (toggle wifi) or enable hotspot on phone
3) Observe SSE close then client reconnect attempt shows 401 with same root request id

Jordan: Can we get full headers for the two connections and compare Authorization jti/jwk? Also need X-Request-Id for both. Customer attached a pcap and an app log.

Tom: Quick client-side mitigation for customer: add an exponential retry on 401 during mid-stream with idempotent resume support; and send a short keepalive ping every 10s to prevent mobile from killing idle sockets. Example client snippet:

```
const es = new EventSource(url, {withCredentials: true});
es.onmessage = (e) => handleChunk(e.data);
es.onerror = (e) => {
  console.log('sse err', e);
  setTimeout(()=> {
    // simple jittered reconnect
    if (lastChunkId) fetch(`${url}?resume_after=${lastChunkId}`, {headers:{Authorization: token}})
  }, 300 + Math.random()*1500);
};
// heartbeat
setInterval(()=> fetch('/_ping',{method:'POST', headers:{Authorization: token}}), 10000);
```

Rene: Server mitigation options:
- accept previous token for N seconds until stream fully terminates (grace window)
- treat in-flight SSE as tied to request-id not token jti for chunk acceptance
- add explicit resume token separate from access token

Jordan: Ops question: does this break any compliance? need signoff. Also add metric for "sse-midstream-401-after-refresh" to monitor.

Amy: Customer asked for ETA. Can eng propose a short-term config fix? They prefer not to ship code.

Rene: Short-term: enable 5s auth grace window for token rotation in infra (config flag). I'll create a rollout PR and diff with flag off by default; can enable for the customer's org id.

Jordan: I'll add an alert and correlate with mobile handoff events in traces. Amy pls collect the request ids and attach to the ticket.

Amy: Will do and ping once I have headers/pcap uploaded. Thanks everyone :thumbsup:

deploy-bot: Rollout PR created: infra/accept-token-grace PR#542 - added feature flag 'auth.token_rotation_grace_seconds'

Amy: Closing loop — customer verified workaround (client keepalive + retry) reduced incidents from 7/day to 1/day. Keeping ticket open for infra change.
